    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d275">

                <pb facs="0500" n="214" xml:id="pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2527</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-23T19:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 23, 1916, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 24, 1.15 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3658. Reichstag postponed discussion of the resolution on submarine warfare in
                    full session; the subject will be discussed in the Budget Committee whose
                    sessions commence next Monday. Cologne <hi rendition="#italic">Gazette</hi>
                    quotes London <hi rendition="#italic">Times</hi> as reporting from Washington
                    that the American Government considers the British instructions to armed
                    merchantmen published by Germany sufficient proof that such vessels are armed
                    for defense only.</p>
                <p>Semiofficially reported that reciprocity agreement has been concluded by Germany
                    with Roumania under which Germany and Austria receive 100,000 wagons of corn and
                    40,000 wagons of grain and malt.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
